    "issue": "Does the British Columbia Utilities Commission have jurisdiction to consider the duty to consult with Aboriginal groups in approving the 2007 Electricity Purchase Agreement (EPA)?",
    "paras": "67-73",
    "applicant_position": "Commission and appellants argue Commission correctly concluded no duty to consider consultation for 2007 EPA.",
    "respondent_position": "CSTC argues Commission erred in refusing to rescope proceeding to allow consultation submissions.",
    "result": "allowed_for_applicant",
    "result_para": 73,
    "result_text": "Commission had power to consider adequacy of Crown consultation under its mandate."
   },
   {
    "issue": "Did the Commission err in refusing to rescope the hearing to include consultation issues regarding the 2007 EPA?",
    "paras": "76-79",
    "applicant_position": "Commission found no adverse impact from 2007 EPA, so no duty to consult triggered; refusal to rescope was correct.",
    "respondent_position": "CSTC argued duty to consult should be considered and hearing rescheduled to include consultation.",
